BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 420.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.77 Tm (The most expensive failure starts before the complaint is filed. Attorney Michael Ehline's opening rule is blunt: don't) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.55 Tm (sue without insurance or a known asset, and remember that a settlement is not a judgment [jPO9_I_LBSw @ 00:00:00].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.32 Tm (Eric Nano of the Sacramento County Public Law Library warns that debtors living off the grid are hard to find, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 352.10 Tm (ones who truly live that way likely have nothing worth collecting anyway [bX8Hhszjuxs @ 00:06:17]. Jeff Leon) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.87 Tm (frames the cost side just as bluntly: weigh the cost of collection, especially on a contingency file, because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.65 Tm (post-judgment fees can exceed what was spent winning the judgment in the first place [R3nWxu374QE @ 00:08:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.42 Tm (The panel boils the whole calculation down to a single line: 'you don't spend a million dollars to collect half a million) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 291.20 Tm (dollars' [R3nWxu374QE @ 00:22:53]. That means every enforcement step needs a projected return attached before it is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.97 Tm (filed, not after the invoices land. The economics check is simple and unforgiving. Before spending a dollar on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.75 Tm (enforcement, know exactly what asset you are chasing, what it will cost to reach it, how long it will take to convert into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.52 Tm (cash, and at what point the file stops being worth another hour of billable work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.30 Tm (The second trap is assuming the debtor will sit still. Tim Anenberger says debtors abscond, transfer, and dissipate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.07 Tm (assets 'all the time,' which is why execution planning, asset mapping, and provisional remedies like attachment belong) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.85 Tm (at the start of the case, before the complaint is even filed, not after the verdict [R3nWxu374QE @ 00:02:25]. Once the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.62 Tm (judgment lands, Tim reports debtors stonewalling and dodging the sheriff for months, and warns that if the debtor files) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.40 Tm (bankruptcy while your judgment sits unrecorded, you are just another unsecured creditor [R3nWxu374QE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.17 Tm (00:45:03]. Private Investigator Videos flags the classic dump: a $100K car sold for $5K is a below-value transfer that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.95 Tm (counts as fraudulent conveyance, and storage units, ATVs, and boats are the targets worth hunting [q-khGCaOPck @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.72 Tm (00:04:52]. Attorney Michael Ehline points to debtors who 'escape' to Florida, citing the OJ and Goldman wrongful) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 108.50 Tm (death case [jPO9_I_LBSw @ 00:00:44]. Each of these moves forces the creditor to spend more just to get back to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 93.27 Tm (where they started. The operator lesson is speed and paper. Record immediately, freeze what you can, and document) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 78.05 Tm (every suspicious transfer before the trail goes cold.) Tj ET
