BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 429.77 Tm (The most common firsthand failure is simply not finding the lien. Hidden Power Files calls the judgment lien one of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 414.55 Tm (most commonly missed instruments in a title search, because it sits in the grantor-grantee index under the debtor's name) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 399.32 Tm (mixed in with deeds, mortgages and releases, and a search that only looks for deed-type entries scans right past it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 384.10 Tm ([-HFzhDO6v-A @ 00:02:02]. Dave at AFX Videos adds that judgment liens are usually not in the land records at all,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 368.87 Tm (yet may affect the property just as much as a mortgage, so anyone ordering a title search should specify that judgment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 353.65 Tm (liens are wanted [a5bLikprQ4E @ 00:01:35]. The reverse trap is a false hit. Realtor Dylan Raquel had a seller, Kristian) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 338.42 Tm (Fuentes, in escrow when the preliminary title report showed a child-support lien against a Christian Fuentes; the seller) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 323.20 Tm (had no kids, filled out a confidential statement of information, and the title insurance company found the Social) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 307.97 Tm (Security numbers did not match and issued a supplement removing the lien [7NXn3JN88l8 @ 00:02:33]. The Raquel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 292.75 Tm (takeaway is that it is not a matter of whether the seller has an issue, but whether anyone with that name has one, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 277.52 Tm (prelim will reveal it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 262.30 Tm (The second trap is economics at the closing table. Tiffany Weber, a real estate attorney in Mooresville, North Carolina,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.07 Tm (sees sellers conceal judgments hoping the closing attorney will not catch them, only for the payoff to surface on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.85 Tm (closing statement with not enough proceeds left, so the seller has to bring money to closing [RFKcDlW0gQU @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 216.62 Tm (00:03:04]. That payoff compounds: David Babel says a judgment docketed in the Bronx Supreme Court attaches to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 201.40 Tm (debtor's property automatically and blocks any refinance or sale until it is paid, including interest accumulating at nine) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 186.17 Tm (percent per year, which over the years can be humongous [q6PjSqG-sF4 @ 00:01:31]. On the creditor's side, the failure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.95 Tm (is attaching to nothing. Kralick warns that a debtor may own real estate without sufficient equity for the lien to attach,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 155.72 Tm (because the property is worth less than what is owed on it; the play then is to wait for improved finances or for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 140.50 Tm (debtor to seek financing [V5NrY_biljg @ 00:02:02]. SpeakLegal lists the three standing problems with any abstract:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 125.27 Tm (finding the county where the debtor owns real estate, secured loans, tax liens and other judgments that come ahead of) Tj ET
