BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (The sharpest split is whether time alone ever frees a debtor once a creditor holds a judgment. Steve Richardson of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (Richardson Law Offices, a southern New Jersey collection defense attorney, tells callers being levied on a ten-year-old) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (judgment that once suit is brought and judgment is entered, the statute of limitations no longer applies and the clock) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (stops ticking [wibZgw9EKZ4 @ 00:00:27]. Weston Legal backs the filing-date rule and kills the process-server dodge:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (the clock stops when the lawsuit is filed, not when you are served, and a judgment can last 20 years in many states) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm ([HD3idZhyATA @ 00:00:48]. Stephen A Williams of The Credit Repair Shop runs the counter-playbook, conceding a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (20-year maximum for a civil judgment but arguing that every state has a dormancy mechanism, and a collector who) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (misses the revival window cannot renew; one Ohio caller faced a revival attempt 12 years into a 10-year revival) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (window, two years past the deadline [--FOsBTlu2E @ 00:04:17]. The Business Guy reads the same map from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (creditor side: California runs 10 years plus a 10-year renewal for a total of 20, while an Oklahoma judgment expires in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (five years but can be renewed every five years indefinitely, so a judgment can sit against a debtor for life [nbtlIEi4we0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (@ 00:02:28].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (State numbers conflict between practitioners, which is why both Williams and Alex Carillo push viewers to check their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (own state before acting. Williams reads Illinois as a seven-year revival window and Georgia as seven years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm ([4Mctc4AuqWA @ 00:03:39], while Carillo of Gustan Cho Associates has heard Illinois runs 20 years and Georgia) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (seven, openly calling those figures guesses and telling viewers to look up the judgment rules where they live) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm ([SvBZyaCOSrc @ 00:01:05]. On federal tax debt the split is tactical rather than numerical. Former IRS agent Mike) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (Sullivan warns that the IRS can extend the 10-year collection clock, or the taxpayer may have extended it already,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (through a bankruptcy, an offer in compromise, an appeals filing, a CDP filing, a lawsuit, time out of the country, or a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (signed waiver [go3rRhIEajA @ 00:01:38]. In a later video Sullivan flatly states the IRS just doesn't extend it on its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (own, and that only some action by the taxpayer extends the statute [0jHEJqFcgLA @ 00:02:56]. Enrolled agent Bob) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (Jablonsky turns the clock into a timing weapon: an offer in compromise can be the best alternative right after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (assessment, but nine years and ten months in, the smarter play is to skip the offer and let the clock expire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm ([KU5hNE5Z2MU @ 00:04:54].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (The defensive playbooks split along wealth lines. The Business Guy pushes an offshore asset protection trust, typically) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (a Cook Islands trust holding an LLC with the firm acting as trustee, because U.S. courts lack jurisdiction over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (foreign trustee, and calls bankruptcy almost always a mistake for anyone with significant assets, since Chapter 7 strips) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (non-exempt assets and a bankruptcy trustee's collection tools are ruthless [5mmy9Xz_Oko @ 00:10:04]. John Skiba of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (Consumer Warrior, with 23 years and over 400 debt collection trials, treats bankruptcy as the nuclear option that stops) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (lawsuits, garnishments, and collections immediately and typically wraps a Chapter 7 in four to five months) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm ([fWHpyqQu_5M @ 00:13:15]. On negotiation, The Business Guy says leverage comes from making collection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (expensive because lawyers love low-hanging fruit, while Consumer Warrior counts settling a $5,000 suit for $800 or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm ($1,000 as a clean win worth chasing before trial [7TbwIGMYgYE @ 00:06:56]. Fight Employment Discrimination) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (adds a courtroom alternative from the EEOC side: an opponent's summary judgment motion forces them to tip their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (hand and show their evidence, and the counter is poking holes in their interpretation of the undisputed facts with your) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (own documents, because neither the judge nor your own attorney will know your file the way you do [X9i8o5iRl9M @) Tj ET
